=== optfil deployment fix: bind mount replaces the symlink ===
Why: filcc-clang-20 resolves its own executable path and requires it to be under the
literal prefix /opt/fil. With /opt/fil as a symlink, /proc/self/exe resolves to the
/home/msaraiva/.local/fil-c/0.685/optfil-0.685-linux-x86_64/opt/fil path, the prefix check fails, and the driver falls back to system
paths (/usr/include, /usr/lib, /lib/ld-fil1-x86_64.so) and fails to link:
  filcc -v shows: -dynamic-linker /lib/ld-fil1-x86_64.so ... /usr/lib/Scrt1.o ... -L/usr/lib
  error: cannot find /usr/lib/Scrt1.o, filc_crt.o, -lc, -lpizlo, -lyolort, ...
With a bind mount, /proc/self/exe stays /opt/fil/bin/filcc-clang-20 and the driver uses
/opt/fil/lib correctly. Physical files remain at the recorded local path.

$ sudo rm /opt/fil            # remove the intermediate symlink we created
$ sudo mkdir /opt/fil
$ sudo mount --bind /home/msaraiva/.local/fil-c/0.685/optfil-0.685-linux-x86_64/opt/fil /opt/fil
rm: cannot remove '/opt/fil': Is a directory
exit_code=0
$ findmnt -no SOURCE,FSTYPE /opt/fil
/dev/nvme0n1p3[/home/msaraiva/.local/fil-c/0.685/optfil-0.685-linux-x86_64/opt/fil] btrfs
/dev/nvme0n1p3[/home/msaraiva/.local/fil-c/0.685/optfil-0.685-linux-x86_64/opt/fil] btrfs
